'''Baliscan Airlines Co., Ltd. (BAL)''' ({{lang-bl|Aerolína Baliscana}}), more commonly known and advertised as '''Baliscana''', is the flag carrier airline of the [[Balisca|Baliscan Confederation]]. The airline is headquartered in the [[Ampurias|Ampurias borough]] of the [[Castejón Metropolis]]. The airline's main hub is Castejón's [[Concordia International Airport]], with secondary hubs at [[Alessandria]]'s [[Novalia International Airport|Novalia Airport]] and [[Bixessarri]]'s [[Isabella Camarasa International Airport|Isabella Camarasa Airport]].

The airline has been owned by the [[Politics of Balisca|Government of Balisca]] from its founding in 1919. The airline has struggled with profitability (largely from competition with the [[AVB|AVB high speed rail system]] for domestic travel). Belief that the airline would not be able to survive the [[W:Impact of the COVID-19 pandemic|impact of the COVID-19 pandemic]] on its own led to government intervention in March 2020. The airline is currently in the midst of a massive restructuring, during which it has been further restricted with the implementation of legislation to "eliminate short-haul flights where trains are available." 
